sentences.l:
But come, mount my chariot, so that you may see
what sort the Trojan horses are, knowing how, over the plain,
very much in a rush, this way and that to pursue and to flee;

“Tydeus’-son Diomedes, made welcome to my heart,
two men I see, strong, eager to fight against you,
having strength immeasurable;

He crashed down from the chariot, and clattered, upon him, his armour,
glancing, all-shining, and swerved aside from him the horses,
swift-footed;

and he took a rock in his hand,
Tydeus’-son, a great work, which not two men could carry,
such as mortals now are;

but he, the hero,
stood on his knees, having crashed down, and propped himself with stout hand
on the earth;

And now there would have perished there the lord of men Aeneas,
if not then sharply had noticed the daughter of Zeus, Aphrodite,
his mother, who to Anchises bore him as he tended cattle;
